# Source pin for Semgrep, the static-analysis scanner run by
# .github/workflows/semgrep.yml. This file lists only the top-level tool; the
# fully resolved, hash-pinned lock that pip actually installs is
# scripts/ci/requirements-semgrep.txt (generated from this file).
#
# semgrep is pinned to an exact version from PyPI, a trusted language package
# registry. The generated lock additionally pins the full transitive closure to
# exact versions and SHA-256 hashes so pip --require-hashes can refuse any
# artifact whose hash does not match (issue #723; same hardening as
# scripts/lint/requirements-lint.txt from issue #699). Pinning the engine version
# does not freeze the rules: the workflow still fetches p/python, p/kotlin, and
# p/security-audit from the Semgrep registry at scan time, so its weekly
# scheduled run keeps picking up newly-published rules.
#
# Regenerating the lock (do this whenever the pin here changes):
#
#   uv pip compile --universal --python-version 3.11 --generate-hashes \
#       scripts/ci/requirements-semgrep.in -o scripts/ci/requirements-semgrep.txt
#
# That command keeps the versions already present in the lock, so on its own it
# only re-resolves what a changed pin in this file forces. Transitive releases
# published since the last run are left alone, including security fixes for
# packages nothing here pins directly (issue #788). Add --upgrade to re-resolve
# the whole closure, or -P/--upgrade-package NAME to move one package and
# whatever it drags with it, which keeps a security bump to a reviewable diff.
#
# --universal + --python-version 3.11 make the lock a superset covering every
# interpreter the install site uses (setup-python's "3.x" in the workflow), so
# every marker-gated and platform-gated entry resolves under --require-hashes.
#
# The floor is 3.11 (issue #1196), so the lock does not cover Python 3.10.
# A package whose newest release dropped 3.10 is locked at that release alone,
# not at two versions under complementary markers, which Dependabot's uv updater
# cannot move (see the uv entry in .github/dependabot.yml).
# Raise the floor again, and regenerate every lock, when packages start dropping
# 3.11; check first that no install site still runs the version being dropped.
semgrep==1.179.0
